# POLICY SECTIONS
# Excerpt of each section (first 500 chars). Full text: USDA_POLICY_SOURCE_FILES_TXT/
# =============================================================================

sections := {
        "1": {
            "title": "Purpose",
            "excerpt": "This Departmental Regulation (DR) establishes rules and guidelines per 29 Code of Federal\n   Regulations (CFR) Part 1614, Federal Sector Equal Employment Opportunity by which the\n   United States Department of Agriculture (USDA or Department) will process administrative\n   complaints of employment discrimination.",
        },
        "2": {
            "title": "Special Instructions/Cancellations",
            "excerpt": "This Regulation replaces DR 4300-007, Processing Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO)\n   Complaints of Discrimination, dated July 12, 2016.",
        },
        "3": {
            "title": "Scope",
            "excerpt": "a.    This DR covers all informal, formal and class complaints of alleged employment\n        discrimination filed by USDA employees, former employees, and applicants for\n        employment against USDA Mission Areas, agencies, and staff offices.\n\n  b.    The DR institutes the provisions of 29 CFR Part 1614 and the U.S. Equal Employment\n        Opportunity Commission’s (EEOC), Equal Employment Opportunity Management\n        Directive 110 (EEO MD-110), Federal Sector Complaints Processing Manual.",
        },
        "4": {
            "title": "Policy",
            "excerpt": "a.    It is USDA’s policy to provide a workplace free from discrimination and harassment\n        based on race, color, national origin, age (40 and older), disability, sex (including\n        pregnancy), protected genetic information, religion, retaliation for engaging in\n        protected activity, political beliefs, or marital, familial or parental status.\n\n  b.    Complaints alleging discrimination on the bases of political beliefs, marital, familial or\n        parental status, and retaliation...",
        },
        "5": {
            "title": "Roles And Responsibilities",
            "excerpt": "a. The Assistant Secretary for Civil Rights (ASCR) will:\n       (1)   Provide leadership;\n       (2)   Provide oversight over all areas of the EEO program;\n       (3)   Exercise authority over all areas of the EEO complaint process for USDA as\n             described below;\n       (4)   Implement the pre-complaint process for staff offices;\n\n\n\n\n                                                2\n      (5) Ensure Mission Areas, agencies, and staff offices follow all civil rights policies,\n         d...",
        },
        "6": {
            "title": "Eeo Complaints",
            "excerpt": "a.   It is USDA’s policy to process all complaints of employment discrimination per 29 CFR\n       Part 1614, EEO MD-110, and this DR. All complaints will be handled in a fair and\n       impartial manner. When a complaint is filed about a matter, all documents relating to\n       the matter will be held by OASCR until the complaint is closed and all rights to appeal\n       have been exhausted.\n\n\n\n\n                                               4\n      Information in a complaint file may be protect...",
        },
        "7": {
            "title": "Conflict Of Interest Complaints",
            "excerpt": "a.   All EEO complaints will be processed without conflicts of interest. USDA will take\n       measures to prevent any such conflicts and, where possible, avoid perceived conflicts of\n       interest. To ensure compliance with this requirement and to maintain the integrity of the\n       EEO complaint program the same official(s) responsible for executing and advising on\n       personnel actions may not also be responsible for managing, advising, or overseeing the\n       EEO pre-complaint or comp...",
        },
        "8": {
            "title": "Class Complaints",
            "excerpt": "a.   A class is a group of employees, former employees, or applicants for employment who,\n       alleged to be or have been adversely affected by a personnel management policy or\n       practice that discriminates against the group based on their race, color, religion, sex, , ,\n       national origin, age, disability, or genetic information.\n\n  b.   A class complaint is a written complaint of discrimination filed on behalf of a class by a\n       class member (agent) who acts for the class during...",
        },
        "9": {
            "title": "Remedies",
            "excerpt": "The policy of the Department is to attempt to make whole any individual who has been found\n  to have suffered from discrimination. The Department will also attempt to resolve\n  complaints, where the Mission Area, agency, or staff office deems it warranted, whether\n  discrimination is explicitly found. Relief, up to and including the maximum possible relief,\n  may be provided by a Mission Area, agency, or staff office to resolve the complaint at any\n  stage.",
        },
        "10": {
            "title": "Right To File A Civil Action",
            "excerpt": "Nothing in this DR will prohibit any aggrieved person or complainant from filing an action in\n  Federal District Court in accordance with the requirements of 29 CFR § 1614.407, Civil\n  Action: Title VII, Age Discrimination in Employment Act, Rehabilitation Act, and the\n  Genetic Information Nondiscrimination Act. However, there are certain bases (marital,\n  familial, or parental status, or political beliefs) that may not be within the jurisdiction of the\n  Federal District Court, if raised as th...",
        },
        "11": {
            "title": "Other Related Provisions",
            "excerpt": "a.   Civil Rights Data Base (DB)\n\n       The ASCR is responsible for and has the authority to administer the Civil Rights DB for\n       the Department. The Civil Rights DB is an electronic computerized system which tracks\n       and provides reports on EEO complaints based on data collected from discrimination\n       complaints filed by USDA employees and applicants for USDA employment.\n\n\n\n\n                                                12\n    b.   Mission Area, Agency, and Staff Office Options...",
        },
        "12": {
            "title": "Inquiries",
            "excerpt": "All USDA Mission Areas, agencies, and staff offices will direct questions and inquiries about\n   this DR to the Center for Civil Rights Operations (CCRO), Compliance Division by email at\n   CCROCompliance@usda.gov.\n\n\n                                              -END-\n\n\n\n\n                                                13\n                                     APPENDIX A\n\n                         ACRONYMS AND ABBREVIATIONS\n\nADR           Alternative Dispute Resolution\nAJ            Administrative...",
        }
}

